  "id": "Compound::DB01078 - Gene::482",
  "verbalization": "Deslanoside appears to interact with Atp1b2 through a series of mechanistic pathways that involve the regulation of sodium-potassium ATPase activity. The evidence suggests that Deslanoside binds to Fxyd2, which is involved in potassium transport, and this interaction leads to the participation of Fxyd2 in potassium-transporting ATPase activity, ultimately resulting in the participation of Atp1b2 in this process. Similarly, Deslanoside's binding to Atp1b1, which is a subunit of the sodium-potassium exchanger, also contributes to the regulation of Atp1b2's activity. These findings indicate that Deslanoside may modulate Atp1b2 through interactions with Fxyd2 or Atp1b1, both of which are critical for the function of the sodium-potassium exchanger. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a robust and reliable relationship, supported by the involvement of Atp1b2 in the regulation of potassium transport. The mechanism appears to involve the modulation of ATPase activity, which is a well-documented pathway in the context of cellular homeostasis and disease.",
